["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/SsvcDecisionType/act", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "The vulnerability requires attention from the organization's internal, supervisory-level and leadership-level individuals. Necessary actions include requesting assistance or information about the vulnerability, as well as publishing a notification either internally and/or externally. Typically, internal groups would meet to determine the overall response and then execute agreed upon actions. CISA recommends remediating Act vulnerabilities as soon as possible.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N9eb3fe323f9b450a9cbc101c666d882d", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/key", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "An ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship describes if a vulnerability is\nlisted in any exploit catalog such as the\nCISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) Catalog <https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog>.\n\n*Constraints*\n\n- The relationship type shall be set to hasAssessmentFor.\n\n*Example*\n\n{\n  \"type\": \"security_ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship\",\n  \"spdxId\": \"urn:spdx.dev:exploit-catalog-1\",\n  \"relationshipType\": \"hasAssessmentFor\",\n  \"security_catalogType\": \"kev\",\n  \"locator\": \"https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog\",\n  \"security_exploited\": \"true\",\n  \"from\": \"urn:spdx.dev:vuln-cve-2023-2136\",\n  \"to\": [\"urn:product-google-chrome-112.0.5615.136\"],\n  \"suppliedBy\": \"urn:spdx.dev:agent-jane-doe\",\n  \"security_publishedTime\": \"2021-03-09T11:04:53Z\"\n}", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Operations/Project", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "Project", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SupplyChain/ResponsibilityType/custody", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "Custody refers to the responsibility, control, and safekeeping of an asset, person, or legal entity. It involves both physical possession and legal authority over something or someone.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Nd28fab3e7b134391b83e94e9f2948dd1", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#maxCount", "1", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer", "", ""]
