["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isni", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "International Standard Name Identifier (ISNI) <https://isni.org/page/what-is-isni/> is a unique identifier used to distinguish the public identities of parties involved in the creation, production, and distribution of media content. Standardized by ISO 27729 <https://www.iso.org/standard/87177.html>, it consists of 16 characters\u201415 digits plus a final check character\u2014and is often represented as a URI, such as https://isni.org/isni/000000012146438X.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ProfileIdentifierType/supplyChain", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "The element follows the SupplyChain profile specification.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N340a9f976ed94af89f8af630f9ba90b0", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest", "_:N0ebc991565684a9f823a4646ad4e5bb6", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SimpleLicensing/licenseExpression", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "A licenseExpression enables the representation, in a single string, of a\ncombination of one or more licenses, together with additions such as license\nexceptions.\n\nThe syntax for a licenseExpression string is set forth in the corresponding\nAnnex of this document\n(\"SPDX license expressions\").\nA licenseExpression string is not valid if it does not conform to the grammar\nset forth in that Annex.\n\nThe ExpandedLicensing profile can be used to represent the complete parsed\nlicense expression as a combination of license objects.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Ne160b65128a8437eb04de500508240a4", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasPrerequisite", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ibid", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "International Business Identifier (IBID) <https://ekys.org/business_identifiers/> is a verifiable unique identifier for legal entities as defined in the ISO/DIS 25500-3 <https://www.iso.org/standard/87705.html> draft standard. It is composed of three data elements: the International Business Registration Number (IBRN), the legal name, and the date of origin formatted as eight numeric characters (YYYYMMDD). Each element is separated by a pipe character (|) (e.g., US-DE.BER:3031657|Code Management Association|19990420).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasRoleIn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The from Element has a role in the to Element. The use of the hasRoleIn is constrained to RoleRelationship classed relationships.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifier", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#NodeShape", "globalId", "", ""]
